# CQ 10: Which functions use no data?
#
# An AI function without data is a function nothing flows through. Clause 5.10
# has the activities of the life cycle transform input data into output data,
# so a function stating none has either not been described or does not belong
# to that chain.
#
# The kind is what tells the two apart. An inference without data is
# incomplete, since it computes a prediction from something. A control, 3.5.5,
# may legitimately state none: it acts on a process rather than on a dataset,
# and the AIAS alignment reaches what it acts on through a relation of its own.
#
# OWL cannot require the data under the open world assumption, so this reports
# where a model has stayed silent rather than where it is wrong.
PREFIX iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?function ?kind ?system
WHERE {
  ?function a ?kind . ?kind rdfs:subClassOf* iso:AIFunction .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?function a ?narrower .
                      ?narrower rdfs:subClassOf+ ?kind ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf* iso:AIFunction }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?function iso:usesData ?any }
  OPTIONAL { ?system iso:hasFunction ?function }
} ORDER BY ?kind ?function
